-- title:
--   Contraction of powers of the Drinfeld-chart centre ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (hypothesis `hqM'`), and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ (`hζ`), and assume (`hι`) that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the subgroup (`hH₁`) cut out as the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(t)\!)$ which (`hK`) is the $L$-subfield generated by the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79).
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain which is a henselian local ring with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$. Let $j \in K$ be the nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`), let $\varpi$ be a generator of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and $j_C :=$ `jChartFin A K j`. Let $y \subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) at which the hypothesis `hss` holds: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_C)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a Drinfeld-chart rigidity package, quantified over all points and summarised here) asserts: for every point $z$ of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) such that the germ at $z$ of $\varpi$ pulled back from the base lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ and satisfying the same supersingularity condition at $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v - fu)$, subject to seven clauses: $e$ carries constants from $A$ to $C(\sigma a)$; every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ attached (in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29)) to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; for such $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ the induced endomorphism of $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; every such $\tau$ acting trivially modulo $y'$ is realised on $S$ by an automorphism $\theta$ fixing constants whose linear part is a matrix $M$ with $M \equiv c\gamma$ and $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, with $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma_{11}\equiv 1 \pmod \ell$ and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ containing $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both variables, and carrying linear forms $(a_1,b_1)$, $(a_2,b_2)$ with $a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ prime to $q$ have distinct contractions to $C$; membership of a contracted prime with linear form $(1,0)$ is described by all Laurent coefficients lying in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $C$, its difference from a suitable constant $a_0 \in A$ lies in $y'$ and has image $mk_S(h)$ for an $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0 \ge 1$, whose leading form is a unit at every pair $(a,b)$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   Now fix such data: a point $z$ of the two-chart integral model, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ (`hy'`), the supersingularity condition `hss'` at $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`). Fix moreover one witness of the above shape: a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and a ring isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$, for which the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts the same seven clauses as above (summarised above) with $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ in place of $W, \sigma, f, u, v, e$.
--
--   Write $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its adic completion, $mk_S$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the ring homomorphism $C \to$ stalk at $z$ obtained from the global-sections isomorphism of $\operatorname{Spec} C$, the inverse of the `appIso` of `ιFin` on the top open, and the germ at $z$ on the open image of `ιFin`. Put $\mathfrak{N} := (mk_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)), mk_S(X_0), mk_S(X_1)) \subseteq S$.
--
--   Finally, let $J \subseteq C$ be the ideal which (`hJ`) is the infimum of all ideals of the form $\mathrm{comap}_{\tau|_C}\big(\mathrm{comap}_{e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC}\circ \mathrm{germY}}(\mathfrak{N})\big)$, taken over $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ which preserve $C$; let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which (`hB`) is generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$; and let $W \subseteq K$ be a valuation subring containing $B$ (`hBW`). Four further hypotheses are imposed. `hR1`: $C \le B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator. `hR2`: $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most one. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $b \in C$, membership in $y$ is equivalent to $b$ lying in $W$ with image in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and $f \in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses): for every $(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose vanishing locus is $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$, which is compatible with $A \to k$ and which, for each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and attached level automorphism $\tau$ preserving $W$, intertwines $\tau$ with [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) at an element $(\overline{\gamma}, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ absorbs the image under some level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ of $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$; an element of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ after all such translations is divisible by $\varpi$; and a level automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is that for every natural number $n$,
--   $$\mathrm{comap}_{e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}}\big(\mathfrak{N}^n\big) = \big(\mathrm{comap}_{e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}}(\mathfrak{N})\big)^n,$$
--   where the contraction is along the composite $C \xrightarrow{\mathrm{germY}} \mathcal{O}_z \xrightarrow{\mathrm{toC}} \widehat{\mathcal{O}_z} \xrightarrow{e_1} S$: the preimage in $C$ of the $n$-th power of the weighted centre $\mathfrak{N}$ of the Drinfeld chart coincides with the $n$-th power of the preimage of $\mathfrak{N}$.
--
--   This is the power-contraction step for the weighted centre of the rigidified supersingular Drinfeld chart in the auxiliary $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-frame, $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$: it says that contraction along the chart map from the complete local ring of the integral model commutes with taking powers of the centre ideal $(\sigma_1\varpi_t, X_0, X_1)$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd), where membership in powers of the centre is detected on the blow-up chart $B$.
